[{"id":"VRCE-3-55-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":1,"english":"Killing the Rākṣasa, Mārīca assuming shapes at will and ranging in the shape of a deer, Rāma vended speedily his way.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"98c322f5c8e718f5d6843ea2ad9380b38179ee162e6949775bcea6ce71c0edb9","compact":"30ced0990dd8eba6e582bde3096a76312535d342c64e70ce39252059f87a1dd0","nasal":"fb798adb60ed96f9fa0e365a30d16e70fd5e5f912d47aa30d075855d2def0f5c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":2,"english":"And as he hurried himself, eager to behold Maithilī, jackals began to howl hideously at his back.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"890229b4f206cc31a9a32e9227476c7a76183fec52d18c7af6564672ef038a38","compact":"607154fc039769d5b7f3d54ea29b75245a26b395231c6d5730769e293ce6278a","nasal":"607154fc039769d5b7f3d54ea29b75245a26b395231c6d5730769e293ce6278a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing their harsh cries, capable of making one's hair stand on end, Rāma struck with fear at the voices of the jackals, became filled with alarm.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fe7f7cbf6436a800327443e51042e9116c88034e890a53f92c5744ebf4c035af","compact":"25515062ac388ed4701fd3722f18516d4a0b83ceca3b7af049ef089d8d0125b1","nasal":"771081bbb40c17b6b124c41792a653c7fb38d6599fa6fa13872a979e8a855d44"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":4,"english":"Ah! I consider this as inauspicious—that these jackals are crying. Escaping being devoured by the Raksasas, may fair fortune befall Vaidehi!","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.773,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e08c179acd4e85b30db8c8d0bf88371a7b631da3502b46b7a2c062d6754723d","compact":"8d927f872f891e15244c06a05f2ac5c0dc43294e9b41a6bca8650802598b9b60","nasal":"8d927f872f891e15244c06a05f2ac5c0dc43294e9b41a6bca8650802598b9b60"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":5,"english":"If Laksmana should have heard the cries which Mārica, knowing my voice, and fixing on the means of harming me, uttered in the form of a deer, Saumitrī, hearing that voice, leaving Mithila's daughter and commissioned by herself, must have come near me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dee2a92e3ff81b3026863fe903a3a8098bf6a6d488e001e80602cb96393c3e12","compact":"fb20a92b11d49fbc0cfb2cabeaf5ccdfaedfde383a9a7389e649ea5921229fe0","nasal":"fb20a92b11d49fbc0cfb2cabeaf5ccdfaedfde383a9a7389e649ea5921229fe0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":6,"english":"If Laksmana should have heard the cries which Mārica, knowing my voice, and fixing on the means of harming me, uttered in the form of a deer, Saumitrī, hearing that voice, leaving Mithila's daughter and commissioned by herself, must have come near me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"442f9736fa78a871fd20d604e02db16e06dc332214d251f6c77b55f676698372","compact":"319223e0b4039abdbe0339d483c5aa8600a3d2b7767e74e8adb82fb8f2036724","nasal":"319223e0b4039abdbe0339d483c5aa8600a3d2b7767e74e8adb82fb8f2036724"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":7,"english":"Surely, the Rākṣasas in a body are desirous of slaying Sitä. Becoming a golden deer, Mārica, having allured me far, transformed himself into a Rākşasa, as soon as he had been struck with my shafts; and exclaimed, 'Ah! Laksmana, slain am I.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.868,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50ba1029d86cc1d57b2ea7cdf6dbca798e6a8f64fca5ebdf5b829cc41e2f22c6","compact":"ab1882c98b2d82305264ee922bb61a5f6e6a19c681f5ea381bbd6d36010e0c45","nasal":"b3d0bc8cceaafb358ef2297425972f6256aa20613826088de0afa5fc7ddf2722"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":8,"english":"Surely, the Rākṣasas in a body are desirous of slaying Sitä. Becoming a golden deer, Mārica, having allured me far, transformed himself into a Rākşasa, as soon as he had been struck with my shafts; and exclaimed, 'Ah! Laksmana, slain am I.'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5f9bb20f0778aa3358757c3694ca62e4cdfa870cc740e9c469c54d87e7650241","compact":"6f6b8010e8741093fccb3f3ad2077fcdb54d9c4957f891b0846a285b92714ef0","nasal":"6f6b8010e8741093fccb3f3ad2077fcdb54d9c4957f891b0846a285b92714ef0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":9,"english":"It is doubtless, we having left (Sītā, whether all is well with her. I having raised the hostility of the Räksasas for the sake of Janasthāna; And many and dreadful are the omens I see (around me). Thus reflecting as he heard the howlings of the jackals, the self-possessed Rāma with hasty steps returned to the asylum.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.663,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-7","DUTT-3-57-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f3887272e4d02a65302efeaea3f24354d21a95f6704145f33d9789e68f3cf23c","compact":"03d107889138dd27f90d18adf656623147af501aa933b6318acd7c00b80b9a95","nasal":"ed8a04a4443848e2800aeac09fbe64b67adafbab3713f138b77c7d86dfd4fa68"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":10,"english":"And many and dreadful are the omens I see (around me). Thus reflecting as he heard the howlings of the jackals, the self-possessed Rāma with hasty steps returned to the asylum. Rāghava went back to Janasthāna, alarmed in consequence of his having been drawn away by the Raksasa in the form of a dear.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.538,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-8","DUTT-3-57-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"142573c92e7c6d825750cec4dfa68864b42638d44b36f11405a97040d1b251b1","compact":"0109e9be38b7f133ca263b04ac62e3b68801ac6c497bed13a1f41625f34c45b1","nasal":"46d6af004cfe5cb99d448d3dff31ba942702334ab33c677d25a23f4c83dc21d6"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":11,"english":"And birds and beasts approached that highsouled one distressed and depressed in spirit; and staying on his left set up frightful cries.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"78e603dff41f5f8afedf108028f64593878fe8ed34edffbed640b477a3e8e5a9","compact":"87939b39e2c63e25bc629d3e962438bc1b4666ee54bc0b31113f536853a3242f","nasal":"87939b39e2c63e25bc629d3e962438bc1b4666ee54bc0b31113f536853a3242f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":12,"english":"As he was witnessing the exceedingly dreadful signs, Rāghava saw Lakşmaņa coming with a lacklustre (countenance); and Lakşmaņa came up to Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49c5b78ee72781e2a1f58e412854c10cc9a67fa31100632a0a0fe2e7f813d5fe","compact":"9ace466f765414b37ff2e1a4676f2a72b5a07431083ea187f4c40808c89688e1","nasal":"81b3c5c960c3c58bc004489dfc80670ce10b18ed8fdc36804adf21f04acd31de"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-55-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":55,"verse":13,"english":"As he was witnessing the exceedingly dreadful signs, Rāghava saw Lakşmaņa coming with a lacklustre (countenance); and Lakşmaņa came up to Rāma. And depressed in spirit, he was rendered still more sad by that one who, afflicted with depression shared his sorrow. And, seeing that (Laksmana) bad come, leaving Sita in that solitary wood frequented by Rākşasas, his brother fell to reprimanding him.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.4,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-57-11","DUTT-3-57-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3055013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fin